--TEST--
A `spawn script` whose argument cannot cross throws in the parent and leaves the parent's value whole: a graph nested past the depth limit and an array holding a callable are each still readable and spawnable afterwards, and each is released once at the end — `rule:classes/graph-copy`, `rule:security/isolate-values-cross-by-copy`
--FILE nvs.toml--
# `spawn script` goes through a door that asks for `script.spawn` first, and
# deny-by-default means a case with no configuration cannot spawn at all.
[capabilities.script]
spawn = true
--FILE depth.nvs--
<?nvs
// Counts how deeply its argument nests.
var $given = Core\Script::args();
int $levels = 0;
while ($given != null && Core\Arr::count($given as array<mixed>) > 0) {
    $given = ($given as array<mixed>)[0];
    $levels = $levels + 1;
}
echo "child counted ", $levels, "\n";
--FILE--
<?nvs
// Past the limit: the refusal is a throw here, before any child exists, and the
// walk that refused it gives back only the reference it was handed.
mixed $deep = [];
int $level = 0;
while ($level < 300) {
    $deep = [$deep];
    $level = $level + 1;
}
try {
    var $refused = spawn script "depth.nvs" with(args: $deep);
    echo "not reached\n";
} catch (LogicError $error) {
    echo "refused: ", Core\Str::contains($error->message, "nests deeper") ? "too deep" : $error->message, "\n";
}

// The parent's value is untouched: walk it, then cut it under the limit and
// send it again. A release too many on the refusal would free it under us.
mixed $walked = $deep;
int $depth = 0;
while (Core\Arr::count($walked as array<mixed>) > 0) {
    $walked = ($walked as array<mixed>)[0];
    $depth = $depth + 1;
}
echo "parent still reads ", $depth, "\n";

mixed $shallow = $deep;
int $cut = 0;
while ($cut < 100) {
    $shallow = ($shallow as array<mixed>)[0];
    $cut = $cut + 1;
}
var $sent = spawn script "depth.nvs" with(args: $shallow, output: "capture");
echo (await $sent)->output;

// A callable is refused as the object it is, one level down.
array<mixed> $withCallable = ["label", fn (): int => 1];
try {
    var $task = spawn script "depth.nvs" with(args: $withCallable);
    echo "not reached\n";
} catch (LogicError $error) {
    echo "refused: a callable\n";
}
echo "parent still holds ", Core\Arr::count($withCallable), " entries\n";
--EXPECT--
refused: too deep
parent still reads 300
child counted 200
refused: a callable
parent still holds 2 entries
